<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Inspect tabs that must not be hosted inside the rebuilt inspect pane.

  This mod normally draws every tab in the pane rather than as a floating window, so that clicking
  along the chip row does not make the panel jump between two shapes. A few tabs cannot survive
  that, and this is the list of them. An excluded tab keeps its chip; clicking it opens the tab's
  own window exactly as it does without this mod.

  Other mods may ship their own copy of this file at
      <YourMod>/Mods/gideon.uioverhaul/InspectTabExclusions.xml
  to exclude their own tabs. Every loaded mod's file is read; ours is read first.

  Set exactly one match key per entry. They are tried most specific first:
      tab        the tab's full type name, namespace included
      namespace  a namespace prefix, for a mod with several tabs that all need excluding
      mod        a packageId, excluding every tab that mod's assemblies define

  When to add an entry. A tab belongs here when it is not really a panel:

    - it sizes itself from the screen rather than from its contents, so hosting it grows the pane
      to fill the screen
    - it draws its own window chrome, background or close button
    - it positions anything in screen coordinates rather than from its own origin

  A tab that is merely large does not belong here. The pane grows to fit and scrolls past that,
  which is the intended behavior.
-->
<Gideon_InspectTabExclusions>

  <entry>
    <tab>Core40k.ITab_RankSystem</tab>
    <reason>Declares its size as the full screen width by the full height above the pane, so hosting it grows the pane to cover the map. It is a full-screen rank tree drawn through the tab system rather than a panel.</reason>
  </entry>

</Gideon_InspectTabExclusions>
